{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"Given that the roots of the polynomial \\(x^5 - 40x^4 + Px^3 + Qx^2 + Rx + S = 0\\) are in geometric progression, let's denote the roots by \\(a, ar, ar^2, ar^3, ar^4\\). By Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots (taken one at a time) is equal to the coefficient of \\(x^4\\) with the opposite sign, which is 40. Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[a + ar + ar^2 + ar^3 + ar^4 = a(1 + r + r^2 + r^3 + r^4) = 40.\\]\n\nNext, we know that the sum of the reciprocals of the roots is 10. The reciprocals of the roots are \\(\\frac{1}{a}, \\frac{1}{ar}, \\frac{1}{ar^2}, \\frac{1}{ar^3}, \\frac{1}{ar^4}\\), and their sum is:\n\n\\[\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{ar} + \\frac{1}{ar^2} + \\frac{1}{ar^3} + \\frac{1}{ar^4} = \\frac{1 + r + r^2 + r^3 + r^4}{a} = 10.\\]\n\nFrom the first equation, we have \\(a(1 + r + r^2 + r^3 + r^4) = 40\\), so we can substitute \\(1 + r + r^2 + r^3 + r^4 = \\frac{40}{a}\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\\frac{\\frac{40}{a}}{a} = 10 \\implies \\frac{40}{a^2} = 10 \\implies a^2 = 4 \\implies a = 2 \\text{ or } a = -2.\\]\n\nWe will consider both cases.\n\n**Case 1: \\(a = 2\\)**\n\n","prefix_end":1046,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[22043,429,279,19703,315,279,47311,17767,87,61,20,481,220,19,15,87,61,19,488,95493,61,18,488,1207,87,61,17,488,35376,488,328,284,220,15,57758,525,304,52484,32724,11,1077,594,78064,279,19703,553,17767,64,11,796,11,796,61,17,11,796,61,18,11,796,61,19,59,568,3216,11401,1915,594,54079,11,279,2629,315,279,19703,320,82161,825,518,264,882,8,374,6144,311,279,35606,315,17767,87,61,19,57758,448,279,14002,1841,11,892,374,220,19,15,13,15277,11,582,614,1447,78045,64,488,796,488,796,61,17,488,796,61,18,488,796,61,19,284,264,7,16,488,435,488,435,61,17,488,435,61,18,488,435,61,19,8,284,220,19,15,7110,2533,5847,11,582,1414,429,279,2629,315,279,24450,27687,1127,315,279,19703,374,220,16,15,13,576,24